\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {40.3}{\ignorespaces The two disjoint cutoff regions fold into the exact coefficient $T_U+T_Y$, followed by the physical cubic matrix on coprime good squarefree ideal factors. Norm axes are schematic, not ideal counts; a common prime gives a raw zero. The displayed tail is the normalized Gauss moment, not an energy or the raw numerator. The bound uses the explicitly cited external cubic sieve. At $U\ge D^{1/8}$ the choice $Y=D^{1/8}$ fits the stated pure critical error budget; if $Y=U$ the coefficient tail is zero. The small-cutoff moment and the full kernel remain open.}}{308}{figure.40.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{gtl:partition}{{40.3}{308}{The two disjoint cutoff regions fold into the exact coefficient $T_U+T_Y$, followed by the physical cubic matrix on coprime good squarefree ideal factors. Norm axes are schematic, not ideal counts; a common prime gives a raw zero. The displayed tail is the normalized Gauss moment, not an energy or the raw numerator. The bound uses the explicitly cited external cubic sieve. At $U\ge D^{1/8}$ the choice $Y=D^{1/8}$ fits the stated pure critical error budget; if $Y=U$ the coefficient tail is zero. The small-cutoff moment and the full kernel remain open}{figure.40.3}{}}
